{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>He divided against them by night.</b> Rashi wrote (Rashi on Genesis 14:15), according to its plain sense, in the manner of pursuers who split up after fugitives when they flee — this one here and this one there. \"By night\" — that is to say, after it grew dark he did not refrain from pursuing them. But the correct interpretation is that he pursued them by day as far as Dan with his entire camp, and when night fell upon them and he could not see which way they would flee, he divided his people and servants into two or three columns, and took one portion with him, and they pursued them along all the roads and struck them as far as Hobah, which is north of Damascus, and he turned back from pursuing them. And its reading is: \"he divided against them, he and his servants, by night.\"" "<b>He pursued them as far as Hobah, which is north of Damascus.</b> It is well known that there is a great distance from the terebinths of Mamre, which are in Hebron in the land of Judah, to Damascus, which is outside the land. If so, he pursued them for many days until he drove them out of the land, for they were returning to Babylonia, their land. Or else it was a great miracle, as our Sages expounded (Genesis Rabbah 43:3) on the verse \"he shall come by foot\" — \"he shall not come\" (Isaiah 41:3)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:21:00.878754386Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}